// Clue - HackSlashInterrogation 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3737889753" "What Hack Slash Knows"
// DetailString :
"P202598862" "Hack Slash doesn't know anything about the Scrapyarders. That was another Freak named Eddie Crush, and he recently went to Paragon City to meet up with another Freakshow gang."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - BashFissionInterrogation 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P402289672" "What Bash Fission Knows"
// DetailString :
"P2011476456" "Bash Fission says that you're too late - some Council already swept in and made off with Eddie Crush. I overheard one of the soldiers say they were taking him back to the Council base on Sharkhead Isle."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - EddieCrushClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1041981828" "What Eddie Crush Knows"
// DetailString :
"P3704107140" "Eddie Crush relates that he was jacking some supplies at the docks when he noticed a boat pull up from the mainland and was met by some Scrapyarders in one of the dockside warehouses. She delivered some supplies to them there, and said how what they did honored the memory of Scrapyard himself. The way she was talking about him, it sounds like she was really friendly with Scrapyard."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - ScrapyarderClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P4082198584" "What the Scrapyarders Know"
// DetailString :
"P977426963" "You drill the Scrapyarder for information, and he grudgingly tells you that they were planning on meeting with their leader on an offshore cargo ship."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - SpinneretteClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2490223462" "Spinnerette's Revelation"
// DetailString :
"P3414904149" "Spinnerette reveals that she took the place of the Scrapyarder leader after she had a premonition of impending danger."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - EpisodeOneClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P50131042" "Freakshow Hideout"
// DetailString :
"P1552872403" "It all started when the old sea captain known as Petrovich asked about helping him track down a valuable piece of information - the identity of the elusive Scrapyarder leader. Word on the street was that some of the Freakshow had a lead on this, so you busted into one of their bases and got one of their bosses, Hack Slash, to spill what he knew. It turns out that that Eddie Crush, another of the Freakshow bosses, just caught the latest ship en route to Paragon City to meet with one of the other Freakshow gangs."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - EpisodeTwoClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1977584211" "Freakshow-Council Rumble"
// DetailString :
"P4130389249" "It all started when the old sea captain known as Petrovich asked about helping him track down a valuable piece of information - the identity of the elusive Scrapyarder leader. Word on the street was that some of the Freakshow had a lead on this, so you busted into one of their bases and got one of their bosses, Hack Slash, to spill what he knew. It turns out that that Eddie Crush, another of the Freakshow bosses, just caught the latest ship en route to Paragon City to meet with one of the other Freakshow gangs.<br><br>Travelling to Paragon City after Eddie Crush, you found that the Freakshow gang in a rumble with a Council assault team. Finding the leader of the Freakshow, you found that you had come to late: Eddie Crush had been taken back to the Council base at Sharkhead Isle for interrogation."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - EpisodeThreeClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1225062445" "Rescuing Eddie Crush"
// DetailString :
"P3109567550" "It all started when the old sea captain known as Petrovich asked about helping him track down a valuable piece of information - the identity of the elusive Scrapyarder leader. Word on the street was that some of the Freakshow had a lead on this, so you busted into one of their bases and got one of their bosses, Hack Slash, to spill what he knew. It turns out that that Eddie Crush, another of the Freakshow bosses, just caught the latest ship en route to Paragon City to meet with one of the other Freakshow gangs.<br><br>Travelling to Paragon City after Eddie Crush, you found that the Freakshow gang in a rumble with a Council assault team. Finding the leader of the Freakshow, you found that you had come to late: Eddie Crush had been taken back to the Council base at Sharkhead Isle for interrogation.<br><br>Back on Sharkhead Isle, you attacked the Council base where they took Eddie Crush, fighting your way through to where Eddie was being interrogated. Eddie agreed to tell you what he knew if you got him out of the base. It turns out Eddie noticed a woman meeting with some Scrapyarders by a warehouse at the docks and delivered them some supplies."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - EpisodeFourClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P586635591" "Family Matters"
// DetailString :
"P2191366582" "It all started when the old sea captain known as Petrovich asked about helping him track down a valuable piece of information - the identity of the elusive Scrapyarder leader. Word on the street was that some of the Freakshow had a lead on this, so you busted into one of their bases and got one of their bosses, Hack Slash, to spill what he knew. It turns out that that Eddie Crush, another of the Freakshow bosses, just caught the latest ship en route to Paragon City to meet with one of the other Freakshow gangs.<br><br>Travelling to Paragon City after Eddie Crush, you found that the Freakshow gang in a rumble with a Council assault team. Finding the leader of the Freakshow, you found that you had come to late: Eddie Crush had been taken back to the Council base at Sharkhead Isle for interrogation.<br><br>Back on Sharkhead Isle, you attacked the Council base where they took Eddie Crush, fighting your way through to where Eddie was being interrogated. Eddie agreed to tell you what he knew if you got him out of the base. It turns out Eddie noticed a woman meeting with some Scrapyarders by a warehouse at the docks and delivered them some supplies.<br><br>Heading over to the warehouse, you found that the Scrapyarders were in conflict with the Family members who owned the place. Fighting through them, you interrogated the Scrapyarder leader, who revealed that they lady they met was on a cargo ship returning to the mainland right now."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - EpisodeFiveClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2513196044" "Spinning the Story"
// DetailString :
"P547852417" "It all started when the old sea captain known as Petrovich asked about helping him track down a valuable piece of information - the identity of the elusive Scrapyarder leader. Word on the street was that some of the Freakshow had a lead on this, so you busted into one of their bases and got one of their bosses, Hack Slash, to spill what he knew. It turns out that that Eddie Crush, another of the Freakshow bosses, just caught the latest ship en route to Paragon City to meet with one of the other Freakshow gangs.<br><br>Travelling to Paragon City after Eddie Crush, you found that the Freakshow gang in a rumble with a Council assault team. Finding the leader of the Freakshow, you found that you had come to late: Eddie Crush had been taken back to the Council base at Sharkhead Isle for interrogation.<br><br>Back on Sharkhead Isle, you attacked the Council base where they took Eddie Crush, fighting your way through to where Eddie was being interrogated. Eddie agreed to tell you what he knew if you got him out of the base. It turns out Eddie noticed a woman meeting with some Scrapyarders by a warehouse at the docks and delivered them some supplies.<br><br>Heading over to the warehouse, you found that the Scrapyarders were in conflict with the Family members who owned the place. Fighting through them, you interrogated the Scrapyarder leader, who revealed that they lady they met was on a cargo ship returning to the mainland right now.<br><br>You headed over to the cargo ship and fought your way past Scrapyarders to discover the woman behind it - only to reveal that she replaced the real Scrapyarder leader at the last minute! Apparently, the Scrapyarder forces got wise to you."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef - SouvenirScrapyardRingSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef Name :
"P3153101378" "Scrapyard's Wedding Ring"
// tDetailString :
"P2798841635" "This is a very nice gold wedding ring worn by the deceased hero known as Scrapyard. You received it from Captain Petrovich in a tale you like to call:<br><br>Iron Widow<br><br>It all started when the old sea captain known as Petrovich asked about helping him track down a valuable piece of information - the identity of the elusive Scrapyarder leader. Word on the street was that some of the Freakshow had a lead on this, so you busted into one of their bases and got one of their bosses, Hack Slash, to spill what he knew. It turns out that that Eddie Crush, another of the Freakshow bosses, just caught the latest ship en route to Paragon City to meet with one of the other Freakshow gangs.<br><br>Travelling to Paragon City after Eddie Crush, you found that the Freakshow gang in a rumble with a Council assault team. Finding the leader of the Freakshow, you found that you had come to late: Eddie Crush had been taken back to the Council base at Sharkhead Isle for interrogation.<br><br>Back on Sharkhead Isle, you attacked the Council base where they took Eddie Crush, fighting your way through to where Eddie was being interrogated. Eddie agreed to tell you what he knew if you got him out of the base. It turns out Eddie noticed a woman meeting with some Scrapyarders by a warehouse at the docks and delivered them some supplies.<br><br>Heading over to the warehouse, you found that the Scrapyarders were in conflict with the Family members who owned the place. Fighting through them, you interrogated the Scrapyarder leader, who revealed that they lady they met was on a cargo ship returning to the mainland right now.<br><br>You headed over to the cargo ship and fought your way past Scrapyarders to discover the woman behind it - only to reveal that she replaced the real Scrapyarder leader at the last minute! Apparently, the Scrapyarder forces got wise to you.<br><br>Returning to Petrovich, you found that the Council managed to secure the real Scrapyarder leader, a woman known as Iron Widow. They were awaiting the arrival of Marshal Brass at their base on Sharkhead Isle, so you had a short time to act. Breaking into the base, you managed to get Iron Widow out of the base where she was taken away by Petrovich's men. Returning to Petrovich one final time, you discovered that he let Iron Widow go! Petrovich tells of how he had failed to prevent Scrapyard's murder at the hands of Captain Mako a while back and decided to make amends by helping Scrapyard's wife, Iron Widow, escape. Bargaining for his life, Petrovich gave you Scrapyard's wedding ring, all that was left of Scrapyard once Captain Mako got through with him."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef - SouvenirScrapyardRingFailure 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// tDetailString :
"P1480124679" "This is a very nice gold wedding ring worn by the deceased hero known as Scrapyard. You received it from Captain Petrovich in a tale you like to call:<br><br>Iron Widow<br><br>It all started when the old sea captain known as Petrovich asked about helping him track down a valuable piece of information - the identity of the elusive Scrapyarder leader. Word on the street was that some of the Freakshow had a lead on this, so you busted into one of their bases and got one of their bosses, Hack Slash, to spill what he knew. It turns out that that Eddie Crush, another of the Freakshow bosses, just caught the latest ship en route to Paragon City to meet with one of the other Freakshow gangs.<br><br>Travelling to Paragon City after Eddie Crush, you found that the Freakshow gang in a rumble with a Council assault team. Finding the leader of the Freakshow, you found that you had come to late: Eddie Crush had been taken back to the Council base at Sharkhead Isle for interrogation.<br><br>Back on Sharkhead Isle, you attacked the Council base where they took Eddie Crush, fighting your way through to where Eddie was being interrogated. Eddie agreed to tell you what he knew if you got him out of the base. It turns out Eddie noticed a woman meeting with some Scrapyarders by a warehouse at the docks and delivered them some supplies.<br><br>Heading over to the warehouse, you found that the Scrapyarders were in conflict with the Family members who owned the place. Fighting through them, you interrogated the Scrapyarder leader, who revealed that they lady they met was on a cargo ship returning to the mainland right now.<br><br>You headed over to the cargo ship and fought your way past Scrapyarders to discover the woman behind it - only to reveal that she replaced the real Scrapyarder leader at the last minute! Apparently, the Scrapyarder forces got wise to you.<br><br>Returning to Petrovich, you found that the Council managed to secure the real Scrapyarder leader, a woman known as Iron Widow. They were awaiting the arrival of Marshal Brass at their base on Sharkhead Isle, so you had a short time to act. Breaking into the base, you attempted to kidnap Iron Widow for yourself but failed to do so before Marshal Brass arrived with his Arachnos troops. You managed to escape, but Iron Widow was captured. Returning to Petrovich one final time, you discovered that he planned to set Iron Widow free! Petrovich tells of how he had failed to prevent Scrapyard's murder at the hands of Captain Mako a while back and decided to make amends by helping Scrapyard's wife, Iron Widow, escape. Bargaining for his life, Petrovich gave you Scrapyard's wedding ring, all that was left of Scrapyard once Captain Mako got through with him."

